1
00:00:05,801 --> 00:00:07,514
(All characters, organizations,
and events in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,539 --> 00:00:09,371
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors. Some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:12,810
(Episode 7)

4
00:00:15,290 --> 00:00:17,011
- Mu Jin.
- Yes?

5
00:00:19,283 --> 00:00:20,856
You know my mom well, don't you?

6
00:00:23,411 --> 00:00:26,176
Back then, eight years ago,

7
00:00:26,911 --> 00:00:28,703
you met my mom, didn't you?

8
00:00:39,263 --> 00:00:40,852
I knew it.

9
00:00:42,651 --> 00:00:44,421
Were you and my mom in love?

10
00:00:46,265 --> 00:00:47,931
Do you still love her?

11
00:00:50,423 --> 00:00:51,641
No.

12
00:00:51,863 --> 00:00:54,267
I'm not interested in married women.

13
00:01:03,037 --> 00:01:04,393
Do you have to get it all over yourself?

14
00:01:11,977 --> 00:01:13,314
You're not having any fries?

15
00:01:14,667 --> 00:01:15,905
Have some fries.

16
00:01:33,195 --> 00:01:39,379
I thought the world was huge,
but it's surprisingly small, isn't it?

17
00:01:46,130 --> 00:01:48,537
Why did you leave Mu Jin,

18
00:01:49,736 --> 00:01:51,159
back then?

19
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:57,153
I'd rather not talk about the past.

20
00:01:58,263 --> 00:01:59,504
All right.

21
00:01:59,627 --> 00:02:02,706
You don't have to answer me.

22
00:02:03,534 --> 00:02:05,371
But I happened...

23
00:02:06,557 --> 00:02:08,545
to find out you'd lied, Gyu Rim.

24
00:02:09,691 --> 00:02:13,216
That you've never been married.

25
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:17,579
That you lied to Mu Jin.

26
00:02:18,224 --> 00:02:21,935
Which means, perhaps,

27
00:02:23,348 --> 00:02:27,690
your son is even more likely,

28
00:02:28,347 --> 00:02:30,953
to be Mu Jin's son.

29
00:02:32,204 --> 00:02:33,838
I really don't want to get involved.

30
00:02:33,863 --> 00:02:36,650
Then don't. It's none of your business.

31
00:02:39,896 --> 00:02:42,836
Mu Jin isn't just anyone to me.

32
00:02:45,283 --> 00:02:49,750
Gyeol has nothing to do with Mu Jin.

33
00:02:49,933 --> 00:02:53,515
You two broke up eight years ago,
and your son is eight.

34
00:02:53,938 --> 00:02:56,937
Anyone who can do basic math
knows that doesn't add up.

35
00:02:59,904 --> 00:03:01,304
I'm sorry,

36
00:03:01,846 --> 00:03:04,887
- but I've heard enough of this nonsense.
- Gyu Rim.

37
00:03:05,665 --> 00:03:07,621
I don't know who gave you the right,

38
00:03:07,706 --> 00:03:11,482
to make assumptions about me.

39
00:03:13,411 --> 00:03:16,868
Stop meddling so carelessly
in another person's life.

40
00:03:17,558 --> 00:03:19,422
We ended a long time ago,

41
00:03:19,776 --> 00:03:22,234
and Gyeol is my son.

42
00:03:22,651 --> 00:03:24,652
He has nothing to do with Mu Jin.

43
00:03:34,909 --> 00:03:36,462
You heard her, Kim Mu Jin.

44
00:03:37,536 --> 00:03:38,949
She says he isn't.

45
00:03:39,971 --> 00:03:43,165
I may not believe it, but you should.

46
00:03:47,850 --> 00:03:49,413
Su Nam, let me do that.

47
00:03:51,079 --> 00:03:53,631
So who was that young man?

48
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:56,409
You looked shocked the second you saw him.

49
00:03:58,142 --> 00:04:02,712
If it's awkward to talk about, never mind.

50
00:04:04,051 --> 00:04:05,947
It's nothing like that. It's just,

51
00:04:06,650 --> 00:04:09,511
someone I knew a while back,
and I ran into him out of nowhere.

52
00:04:11,404 --> 00:04:16,158
I thought he might be an old flame
of yours, Gyu Rim.

53
00:04:16,271 --> 00:04:17,875
That's right.

54
00:04:18,785 --> 00:04:23,638
Honestly, as your old flame,
he was a bit underwhelming.

55
00:04:23,821 --> 00:04:26,334
That face, that build.

56
00:04:26,741 --> 00:04:31,248
A man who's tall but has nothing else
going for him is boring.

57
00:04:31,273 --> 00:04:33,541
Not one bit of use.

58
00:04:33,828 --> 00:04:35,904
A real man,

59
00:04:35,929 --> 00:04:39,745
should be short and sturdy
like my Heung Sik,

60
00:04:39,771 --> 00:04:43,621
and strong enough
to take care of his family.

61
00:04:44,478 --> 00:04:45,846
Isn't that right?

62
00:04:48,077 --> 00:04:49,364
That's right. Right?

63
00:04:49,445 --> 00:04:54,618
Exactly. My Heung Sik.
Isn't he here yet? Closing up...

64
00:05:12,124 --> 00:05:13,284
What's that?

65
00:05:14,191 --> 00:05:15,691
A straw Gyeol used.

66
00:05:17,530 --> 00:05:21,118
What for? Are you actually running
a paternity test?

67
00:05:22,058 --> 00:05:26,184
And what if he really is your son?

68
00:05:27,052 --> 00:05:28,394
Exactly.

69
00:05:29,365 --> 00:05:30,712
What am I supposed to do?

70
00:05:31,510 --> 00:05:35,679
Take him away from Gyu Rim?
Or start over with Gyu Rim...

71
00:05:38,731 --> 00:05:41,193
Get her divorced and marry her?

72
00:05:42,843 --> 00:05:44,094
No.

73
00:05:45,364 --> 00:05:48,153
I have no right to. By what right?

74
00:05:49,538 --> 00:05:50,971
I'm not a stalker.

75
00:05:51,091 --> 00:05:54,567
I have no right to come crashing
into Han Gyu Rim's life like this,

76
00:05:56,536 --> 00:05:57,757
and turn it upside down.

77
00:05:58,913 --> 00:06:00,361
You've come to your senses.

78
00:06:03,031 --> 00:06:04,232
Let's throw this away.

79
00:06:08,110 --> 00:06:09,257
My friend.

80
00:06:10,255 --> 00:06:13,361
You're truly back to normal.
I'm incredibly glad.

81
00:06:13,844 --> 00:06:16,528
Right. Let's stop here.

82
00:06:17,442 --> 00:06:20,882
Good call. Forget her cleanly.
Let's put it behind us.

83
00:06:21,044 --> 00:06:23,689
Han Gyu Rim has the right
to be forgotten by you.

84
00:06:55,051 --> 00:06:56,454
What are you doing alone in the dark?

85
00:06:58,494 --> 00:06:59,978
I'm thinking something over.

86
00:07:01,690 --> 00:07:02,876
Thinking what over?

87
00:07:03,411 --> 00:07:04,947
It's a thing.

88
00:07:06,204 --> 00:07:08,451
Can I solve it or not?

89
00:07:09,404 --> 00:07:10,709
You can't.

90
00:07:10,893 --> 00:07:12,244
You won't even tell me.

91
00:07:13,410 --> 00:07:16,440
Gyu Seo, it's about someone
that you wouldn't know.

92
00:07:17,596 --> 00:07:20,047
Actually, maybe you would know.

93
00:07:20,177 --> 00:07:21,737
You've lived longer than I have.

94
00:07:21,844 --> 00:07:23,445
What is it? Who?

95
00:07:24,913 --> 00:07:28,113
Never mind. Forget it and go study.

96
00:07:28,951 --> 00:07:30,171
All right.

97
00:07:30,557 --> 00:07:33,909
Then I'll leave it alone and study.
You can keep racking your brain.

98
00:07:37,437 --> 00:07:39,219
As if I would.

99
00:07:40,158 --> 00:07:43,491
You take far too much interest in me.
It's a problem.

100
00:07:43,897 --> 00:07:45,194
So what is it?

101
00:07:48,804 --> 00:07:52,640
The man Mom liked eight years ago
has turned up again.

102
00:07:52,793 --> 00:07:53,858
Eight years ago?

103
00:07:54,411 --> 00:07:55,678
Eight years ago,

104
00:07:56,671 --> 00:07:57,972
you mean Mu Jin?

105
00:07:58,364 --> 00:08:00,776
- You know him?
- Of course I do.

106
00:08:00,887 --> 00:08:04,581
When we were little, he bought us treats
and took us for photo booths.

107
00:08:05,104 --> 00:08:06,840
Mu Jin has turned up again?

108
00:08:07,858 --> 00:08:09,966
Where is he now? Does Gyu Rim know?

109
00:08:10,024 --> 00:08:13,423
Did she meet him? What did she say?
Was she very shocked?

110
00:08:15,608 --> 00:08:17,411
The man Gyu Rim used to date?

111
00:08:21,256 --> 00:08:22,519
Who told you that?

112
00:08:22,544 --> 00:08:25,268
Gyeol. They met while gaming,

113
00:08:25,408 --> 00:08:27,139
and now Gyeol says Mu Jin
is his best friend.

114
00:08:27,361 --> 00:08:29,078
Where is he now?

115
00:08:29,479 --> 00:08:31,798
Wait, does Gyu Rim know?

116
00:08:31,823 --> 00:08:34,454
Did she meet him? What did she say?

117
00:08:34,855 --> 00:08:36,312
She must have been so shocked.

118
00:08:36,738 --> 00:08:38,484
Didn't she cry?

119
00:08:38,804 --> 00:08:40,490
We're definitely twins.

120
00:08:43,004 --> 00:08:45,104
Gyu Rim can't go through that again.

121
00:08:46,051 --> 00:08:48,011
Did Mu Jin put Gyu Rim through something?

122
00:08:50,091 --> 00:08:51,312
It's a thing.

123
00:08:52,203 --> 00:08:53,953
So what is "a thing?"

124
00:08:55,084 --> 00:08:57,023
Kids don't need to know.

125
00:09:00,344 --> 00:09:02,374
What are we going to do about her?

126
00:09:02,977 --> 00:09:08,994
(Suragan Side Dishes)

127
00:09:11,887 --> 00:09:13,112
Gyu Rim.

128
00:09:14,934 --> 00:09:16,301
Heung Sik.

129
00:09:17,602 --> 00:09:20,495
Su Nam had business in Majang Dong,
so she left early.

130
00:09:21,691 --> 00:09:24,869
I didn't come to see my mom.
I came to see you.

131
00:09:25,495 --> 00:09:26,560
Me?

132
00:09:26,592 --> 00:09:29,239
I think I ought to tell you.

133
00:09:31,021 --> 00:09:35,131
Today I walked straight into Gyeol's trap.

134
00:09:35,610 --> 00:09:37,423
What do you mean?

135
00:09:37,486 --> 00:09:40,859
Well, the thing is...

136
00:09:41,815 --> 00:09:45,625
That you and Kim Mu Jin
were in love back then,

137
00:09:46,364 --> 00:09:47,720
Gyeol found out.

138
00:09:48,081 --> 00:09:49,350
What?

139
00:09:49,526 --> 00:09:52,438
That little boy is way too clever...

140
00:09:52,671 --> 00:09:54,879
No. It's this mouth of mine.

141
00:09:55,437 --> 00:09:59,169
My mouth is the problem.
What am I to do with this mouth?

142
00:10:00,605 --> 00:10:02,577
I'm truly sorry, Gyu Rim.

143
00:10:07,964 --> 00:10:11,021
Were you and my mom in love?

144
00:10:19,721 --> 00:10:21,355
Do you still love her?

145
00:10:40,243 --> 00:10:43,500
Mom, are you angry with me
about something?

146
00:10:46,884 --> 00:10:49,194
Why haven't you looked at me
since yesterday?

147
00:10:55,828 --> 00:10:58,120
I asked if you're angry with me.

148
00:11:03,488 --> 00:11:05,578
Why are you digging into my past?

149
00:11:07,198 --> 00:11:08,843
Is that what you're angry about?

150
00:11:09,058 --> 00:11:11,016
If you're curious, ask me,

151
00:11:11,203 --> 00:11:12,933
instead of pestering Heung Sik.

152
00:11:12,983 --> 00:11:16,266
You wouldn't tell me the truth
if I asked you.

153
00:11:21,993 --> 00:11:26,450
And you lied about knowing Mu Jin,
when you two clearly know each other.

154
00:11:34,951 --> 00:11:37,815
You used to hate it,

155
00:11:37,904 --> 00:11:39,808
whenever another man
showed interest in me.

156
00:11:41,833 --> 00:11:44,790
You said even Kim Woo Bin
wasn't good enough for me.

157
00:11:45,042 --> 00:11:47,003
- Am I right or wrong?
- Right.

158
00:11:47,272 --> 00:11:49,530
So why are you so warm toward Mu Jin?

159
00:11:50,131 --> 00:11:52,169
Is it because he sent you game items?

160
00:11:56,191 --> 00:11:59,142
Because I'd like to have a dad now too.

161
00:12:01,594 --> 00:12:06,467
I can't stand listening to Cheol Gi
brag about his dad anymore,

162
00:12:06,523 --> 00:12:11,230
and I can't take the kids teasing me
about not having a dad either.

163
00:12:12,584 --> 00:12:16,424
But Mu Jin says he isn't
interested in you.

164
00:12:17,387 --> 00:12:20,004
He says he isn't interested
in married women.

165
00:12:22,351 --> 00:12:25,356
He's the only man I've ever liked
in my whole life,

166
00:12:25,803 --> 00:12:27,327
so what are you going to do now?

167
00:13:11,159 --> 00:13:12,587
Honestly.

168
00:13:12,691 --> 00:13:15,471
I walked out like that,
and not one of them...

169
00:13:15,502 --> 00:13:16,926
even called or texted me?

170
00:13:16,951 --> 00:13:18,438
And you call yourselves family?

171
00:13:18,907 --> 00:13:22,228
Fine. I'm done too.

172
00:13:22,253 --> 00:13:24,228
I'm finished with the wretched Han family.

173
00:13:26,684 --> 00:13:29,476
I heard you asked my husband
to come to the wedding as well.

174
00:13:30,659 --> 00:13:31,956
That can't happen.

175
00:13:33,315 --> 00:13:34,953
I won't let him go.

176
00:14:04,226 --> 00:14:05,611
Have a seat. Make yourself comfortable.

177
00:14:11,298 --> 00:14:13,833
- Gyu Yeong, what are you doing?
- Please help me.

178
00:14:14,545 --> 00:14:16,052
Just once more, please help me.

179
00:14:18,583 --> 00:14:19,871
Get up, quickly.

180
00:14:20,251 --> 00:14:21,771
If you help me just once more,

181
00:14:22,111 --> 00:14:24,452
I'll never contact you again
about anything.

182
00:14:24,991 --> 00:14:28,052
Even if we pass on the street,
I'll walk by like a stranger.

183
00:14:28,077 --> 00:14:30,037
Whatever this is about...

184
00:14:30,478 --> 00:14:33,497
Get up first. Let's sit down and talk.

185
00:14:34,531 --> 00:14:38,036
I won't get up until you promise me.

186
00:14:41,757 --> 00:14:43,622
What is it I'm meant to promise?

187
00:14:46,949 --> 00:14:49,041
Come to my wedding just once.

188
00:14:49,961 --> 00:14:51,693
Just this once, please.

189
00:14:55,590 --> 00:14:58,583
I was going to contact you anyway.

190
00:14:59,117 --> 00:15:01,517
Could I get your in-laws' contact details?

191
00:15:02,491 --> 00:15:03,816
What for?

192
00:15:04,461 --> 00:15:07,341
To apologize now, before it's too late.

193
00:15:07,591 --> 00:15:09,825
If something's wrong,
we should make it right.

194
00:15:10,246 --> 00:15:12,999
- Let's do that.
- Sir.

195
00:15:13,106 --> 00:15:17,826
Ever since that family meeting
I've felt uneasy and troubled.

196
00:15:18,584 --> 00:15:19,860
All right, fine.

197
00:15:20,036 --> 00:15:22,113
I know I had no choice but to go,

198
00:15:22,724 --> 00:15:25,631
but no matter how many times
I think it over, this isn't right.

199
00:15:26,464 --> 00:15:30,444
So I'll meet your in-laws,

200
00:15:30,859 --> 00:15:34,392
explain the circumstances, and apologize.

201
00:15:35,396 --> 00:15:37,916
How exactly will you explain
and how will you apologize?

202
00:15:38,958 --> 00:15:40,145
I'll handle that myself...

203
00:15:40,189 --> 00:15:42,891
"I got caught up with a con artist
and ended up in a mess."

204
00:15:43,147 --> 00:15:45,968
So you'll just come clean
and be done with it?

205
00:15:46,171 --> 00:15:47,623
That isn't what I meant.

206
00:15:47,671 --> 00:15:49,004
Then what about me?

207
00:15:49,021 --> 00:15:51,338
Do you think my in-laws will say,
"We understand."

208
00:15:51,354 --> 00:15:53,517
"So that's what happened."
"She must have been desperate."

209
00:15:54,331 --> 00:15:55,875
And simply let it go?

210
00:15:56,011 --> 00:15:57,338
Gyu Yeong.

211
00:15:57,799 --> 00:16:00,827
You introducing me as your father
wasn't exactly a lie,

212
00:16:01,319 --> 00:16:04,571
and yes, of course, having two fathers,

213
00:16:04,848 --> 00:16:06,638
isn't your fault either.

214
00:16:08,071 --> 00:16:09,604
Don't worry too much.

215
00:16:10,381 --> 00:16:13,416
If I explain it properly,
they'll understand.

216
00:16:15,143 --> 00:16:17,324
If you won't help, don't wreck it either.

217
00:16:19,831 --> 00:16:21,571
- Gyu Yeong.
- If...

218
00:16:22,571 --> 00:16:24,304
my marriage falls apart because of you,

219
00:16:24,831 --> 00:16:26,517
I won't take it quietly.

220
00:16:27,811 --> 00:16:29,985
Whose fault is it that my life
turned out this way?

221
00:16:30,511 --> 00:16:32,204
She had us because she wanted to,

222
00:16:32,675 --> 00:16:35,290
then ran off and left her children
to live well on her own.

223
00:16:35,888 --> 00:16:38,406
Do you think I'll just stand by and watch?

224
00:17:36,771 --> 00:17:39,471
(Emigrating to the United States)

225
00:17:46,204 --> 00:17:48,356
Is your stomach any better?

226
00:17:49,417 --> 00:17:51,959
You had a fever last night.

227
00:17:52,714 --> 00:17:54,125
I'm fine.

228
00:17:55,504 --> 00:17:56,821
Let me see.

229
00:17:59,698 --> 00:18:01,040
You're fine.

230
00:18:02,050 --> 00:18:03,957
What are you reading so intently?

231
00:18:05,994 --> 00:18:07,028
Emigrating to the United States...

232
00:18:09,554 --> 00:18:11,054
Even the United States is close.

233
00:18:11,054 --> 00:18:12,354
Which country is farther?

234
00:18:12,867 --> 00:18:15,514
- Are you really emigrating?
- Yes.

235
00:18:19,491 --> 00:18:22,254
Why? Because of Mu Jin?

236
00:18:23,674 --> 00:18:27,702
I'm tired of spending 23 years loving
a man who doesn't see me as a woman.

237
00:18:28,054 --> 00:18:30,908
I think I should leave
and stop putting myself through this.

238
00:18:31,940 --> 00:18:33,440
Han Gyu Rim...

239
00:18:33,513 --> 00:18:36,061
I hate her, but I truly envy her.

240
00:18:38,521 --> 00:18:39,587
Who?

241
00:18:40,587 --> 00:18:41,654
Who did you say?

242
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:43,154
Han Gyu Rim.

243
00:18:43,587 --> 00:18:45,587
She's the woman Mu Jin was with.

244
00:18:49,114 --> 00:18:51,363
Why? Do you know her?

245
00:18:51,787 --> 00:18:53,021
No.

246
00:18:54,588 --> 00:18:56,888
How old is she?

247
00:18:57,787 --> 00:18:59,054
About my age, I think.

248
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:03,241
Where...

249
00:19:04,821 --> 00:19:06,421
What neighborhood does she live in?

250
00:19:06,987 --> 00:19:08,354
I don't know that either.

251
00:19:09,121 --> 00:19:12,037
Why? Are you going to go
and tear her hair out?

252
00:19:17,506 --> 00:19:20,706
Seven items, 23 dollars in total.

253
00:19:21,021 --> 00:19:22,821
The potato salad is on the house.

254
00:19:22,821 --> 00:19:24,263
Thank you.

255
00:19:31,021 --> 00:19:32,754
You must be a mother and daughter.

256
00:19:32,754 --> 00:19:34,721
You two look so much alike.

257
00:19:35,673 --> 00:19:36,706
Here you go.

258
00:19:36,987 --> 00:19:39,154
We're not. I'm far prettier.

259
00:19:39,154 --> 00:19:40,762
This girl.

260
00:19:41,427 --> 00:19:43,523
- Good luck with sales.
- Yes, take care.

261
00:19:44,187 --> 00:19:47,100
- Amazing, we even got a freebie.
- It looks delicious.

262
00:19:47,354 --> 00:19:49,154
- This looks so good too.
- Yes.

263
00:19:52,721 --> 00:19:53,721
Envious?

264
00:19:54,687 --> 00:19:55,787
No.

265
00:19:56,454 --> 00:19:58,354
Don't you miss your mother?

266
00:20:00,554 --> 00:20:03,221
Your mother is a hard one.

267
00:20:03,747 --> 00:20:07,987
Even after remarrying,
she could've visited at least once.

268
00:20:09,054 --> 00:20:10,821
As long as she's living well,
that's enough for me.

269
00:20:11,787 --> 00:20:13,521
Were there no delivery orders today?

270
00:20:13,921 --> 00:20:16,229
Of course there were. We're busy.

271
00:20:16,254 --> 00:20:18,511
Orders are piling up. Come on, hurry.

272
00:20:19,154 --> 00:20:20,654
Let's trim these spring onions.

273
00:20:23,587 --> 00:20:25,787
How was the recipe I sent you last time?

274
00:20:26,887 --> 00:20:28,287
Was it good?

275
00:20:28,639 --> 00:20:29,821
Did people like it?

276
00:20:32,821 --> 00:20:34,754
Nice. Good to hear that.

277
00:20:36,321 --> 00:20:37,721
Your recipe?

278
00:20:37,887 --> 00:20:40,021
I told you, it was awesome.

279
00:20:45,954 --> 00:20:46,954
Okay.

280
00:20:48,521 --> 00:20:50,354
Take care. See you.

281
00:20:52,994 --> 00:20:54,521
Suragan Side Dishes is so much better,

282
00:20:54,521 --> 00:20:55,921
so why are we back to Mom's Side Dishes?

283
00:20:56,187 --> 00:20:57,187
Exactly.

284
00:20:57,212 --> 00:21:00,221
The reviews say their greens
and side dishes are the best,

285
00:21:00,221 --> 00:21:02,221
and the pancakes and stews
are even better.

286
00:21:02,246 --> 00:21:05,687
Our CEO says never to order
from Suragan, so what can we do?

287
00:21:06,021 --> 00:21:08,876
And he was the one who said
he wanted to relabel it and sell it.

288
00:21:09,587 --> 00:21:12,287
I think there's something
between him and Mom's Side Dishes.

289
00:21:12,554 --> 00:21:14,621
Why? Did he take a bribe?

290
00:21:15,787 --> 00:21:17,054
No, it's not that...

291
00:21:19,121 --> 00:21:20,421
What are they going on about?

292
00:21:20,421 --> 00:21:22,154
And what's Suragan?

293
00:21:22,439 --> 00:21:25,787
There's a side dish shop
we started ordering from recently.

294
00:21:25,787 --> 00:21:28,562
Their food is so good
that everyone loved it.

295
00:21:28,587 --> 00:21:29,587
Yes.

296
00:21:29,612 --> 00:21:32,987
But the CEO suddenly said
we absolutely can't order there...

297
00:21:33,054 --> 00:21:34,087
Why not?

298
00:21:34,496 --> 00:21:37,129
Isn't that the place you said
was incredible last time?

299
00:21:37,214 --> 00:21:39,603
- The one you wanted me to try?
- Yes.

300
00:21:40,321 --> 00:21:41,787
Is it really that good?

301
00:21:41,787 --> 00:21:43,121
- It's amazing.
- It's amazing.

302
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:45,040
Chef, you really have to try it.

303
00:21:46,454 --> 00:21:48,621
We have some Suragan side dishes
left in the fridge.

304
00:21:48,621 --> 00:21:50,492
- Would you like a taste?
- Sure, bring it over.

305
00:21:50,517 --> 00:21:51,517
Yes.

306
00:21:52,047 --> 00:21:54,534
If he's taking bribes, I'll fire him.

307
00:21:54,587 --> 00:21:57,104
- The CEO?
- What's a CEO?

308
00:21:57,221 --> 00:21:58,987
You lot just have to rise up.

309
00:21:59,187 --> 00:22:00,454
"For our one staff meal a day,"

310
00:22:00,454 --> 00:22:03,021
"we demand the side dishes
we want." There you go.

311
00:22:03,154 --> 00:22:05,487
Chef, shouldn't you run for office?

312
00:22:05,574 --> 00:22:08,262
But if those side dishes aren't good,
I'll fire all of you.

313
00:22:08,287 --> 00:22:09,954
For daring to slander the CEO.

314
00:22:09,954 --> 00:22:11,854
- Yes, we're confident.
- Of course.

315
00:22:12,554 --> 00:22:13,587
Chef.

316
00:22:14,387 --> 00:22:15,487
Please have a taste.

317
00:22:15,654 --> 00:22:16,721
- Is this it?
- Yes.

318
00:22:20,287 --> 00:22:21,487
With the kimchi...

319
00:22:40,487 --> 00:22:41,754
This is good.

320
00:22:43,041 --> 00:22:44,953
It's really good.

321
00:22:45,321 --> 00:22:46,587
How did you find this place?

322
00:22:46,987 --> 00:22:48,087
It was easy.

323
00:22:49,287 --> 00:22:51,662
- Where's Park Jeong Woo now?
- He's in the office.

324
00:22:51,754 --> 00:22:52,854
That guy.

325
00:22:58,154 --> 00:22:59,187
Sir.

326
00:22:59,854 --> 00:23:01,187
You'd best leave at once.

327
00:23:01,687 --> 00:23:03,321
The people are rising up.

328
00:23:03,421 --> 00:23:04,621
What are you talking about?

329
00:23:04,787 --> 00:23:05,887
You.

330
00:23:05,887 --> 00:23:08,121
Why won't you let them switch
to a side dish shop,

331
00:23:08,121 --> 00:23:09,254
that everyone loves?

332
00:23:09,854 --> 00:23:11,974
- What kind of dictatorship is that?
- What are you...

333
00:23:13,987 --> 00:23:15,254
Suragan...

334
00:23:16,621 --> 00:23:17,821
That place tastes terrible.

335
00:23:18,154 --> 00:23:20,754
But you were the one who raved
about that place last time.

336
00:23:21,314 --> 00:23:25,182
I had it a few times,
and it's loaded with MSG. Bad for health.

337
00:23:25,554 --> 00:23:26,854
I tried it myself.

338
00:23:27,121 --> 00:23:28,621
I didn't taste any additives at all.

339
00:23:30,554 --> 00:23:32,154
The owner is unfriendly.

340
00:23:32,721 --> 00:23:34,554
They're doing so well that they
don't give anything extra,

341
00:23:34,554 --> 00:23:36,021
and I think their portions are small too.

342
00:23:36,021 --> 00:23:37,987
Mom's Side Dishes gives twice as much
for the same money.

343
00:23:38,821 --> 00:23:39,987
Really?

344
00:23:42,021 --> 00:23:43,387
I'd better go and see for myself.

345
00:23:43,687 --> 00:23:45,287
Freeze.

346
00:23:45,737 --> 00:23:48,129
Why would you go there?

347
00:23:48,154 --> 00:23:49,254
Do you have that much free time?

348
00:23:51,321 --> 00:23:52,687
You're getting more suspicious.

349
00:23:53,021 --> 00:23:54,595
Suspicious? What's suspicious?

350
00:23:55,787 --> 00:23:56,954
Move aside.

351
00:23:57,921 --> 00:23:59,354
Do you trust me that little?

352
00:24:00,021 --> 00:24:02,787
Do I need your permission
for every side dish shop the staff use?

353
00:24:02,812 --> 00:24:04,921
If that's how it is, you be the CEO.

354
00:24:05,521 --> 00:24:07,021
You know you're acting strange, right?

355
00:24:07,021 --> 00:24:08,987
I don't. What's strange about it?

356
00:24:09,554 --> 00:24:12,321
If I knew everything, would I be a CEO
with no say in anything?

357
00:24:13,454 --> 00:24:14,654
There you go again.

358
00:24:15,987 --> 00:24:17,087
Move.

359
00:24:17,554 --> 00:24:18,821
Really, don't go.

360
00:24:27,354 --> 00:24:28,521
What's that smell?

361
00:24:43,673 --> 00:24:44,790
What are you doing?

362
00:24:45,854 --> 00:24:47,287
You're up?

363
00:24:48,521 --> 00:24:51,021
I'm making those sweet potato
fritters that you like.

364
00:24:54,347 --> 00:24:55,414
That's hot.

365
00:24:55,954 --> 00:24:57,154
Move aside.

366
00:24:57,721 --> 00:24:59,454
Look at you, doing something you never do.

367
00:24:59,687 --> 00:25:00,721
Come here.

368
00:25:01,585 --> 00:25:04,387
I was trying to make them really good
for you.

369
00:25:05,954 --> 00:25:07,887
You love sweet potato fritters,
don't you, Gyu O?

370
00:25:08,187 --> 00:25:09,421
I don't.

371
00:25:10,187 --> 00:25:13,521
You used to love sweet potato fritters.

372
00:25:15,027 --> 00:25:16,093
Go stand over there.

373
00:25:18,087 --> 00:25:19,754
That would be Han Gyu Yeong.

374
00:25:22,521 --> 00:25:23,754
Then do you like potatoes?

375
00:25:24,554 --> 00:25:26,721
Shall I buy some and make you fries?

376
00:25:26,721 --> 00:25:28,254
I don't like potatoes either.

377
00:25:28,754 --> 00:25:30,254
Really? Then...

378
00:25:30,954 --> 00:25:31,987
Corn?

379
00:25:33,654 --> 00:25:35,954
Carrots, maybe.

380
00:25:36,787 --> 00:25:39,787
Cucumber? Onion? What shall I make?

381
00:25:44,021 --> 00:25:45,154
Do you need money again?

382
00:25:46,154 --> 00:25:48,154
What do you take me for?

383
00:25:49,054 --> 00:25:51,287
I'm doing this for you.

384
00:25:51,287 --> 00:25:53,187
I even burned my arm doing this for you,

385
00:25:53,187 --> 00:25:55,321
trying to make your favorite food,
and earlier...

386
00:25:55,654 --> 00:25:57,954
I even cut my finger
slicing sweet potatoes.

387
00:25:59,141 --> 00:26:02,054
So why are you suddenly like this?

388
00:26:02,454 --> 00:26:05,054
It isn't sudden.

389
00:26:05,580 --> 00:26:07,514
The feeling was always there.

390
00:26:07,754 --> 00:26:09,221
You don't know it,

391
00:26:09,221 --> 00:26:12,465
but I'm actually pretty fatherly.

392
00:26:13,754 --> 00:26:14,954
Are you okay?

393
00:26:15,321 --> 00:26:17,254
Are you dying soon or something?

394
00:26:17,734 --> 00:26:19,900
The things you say...

395
00:26:26,421 --> 00:26:28,437
After watching the kids fight yesterday,

396
00:26:30,021 --> 00:26:32,454
I couldn't sleep a wink all night.

397
00:26:34,154 --> 00:26:39,175
I looked back slowly over the life
I've lived until now,

398
00:26:40,674 --> 00:26:42,540
and it was all my doing,

399
00:26:43,454 --> 00:26:44,721
all my fault.

400
00:26:45,682 --> 00:26:49,454
I was never much of a father to you.

401
00:26:50,171 --> 00:26:53,162
So from now on I'm going to do
everything for you,

402
00:26:53,187 --> 00:26:55,654
everything I should've done but never did,

403
00:26:56,821 --> 00:26:58,987
and spend some time making amends.

404
00:26:58,987 --> 00:27:01,821
You never thought like
that your whole life,

405
00:27:03,054 --> 00:27:04,721
and now this suddenly?

406
00:27:05,021 --> 00:27:07,087
Dad, are you seriously sick?

407
00:27:07,514 --> 00:27:09,514
They say a sudden change
means you're dying.

408
00:27:11,021 --> 00:27:12,887
This boy, honestly.

409
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:14,340
What?

410
00:27:14,387 --> 00:27:16,421
Would you be happy if I got really sick,

411
00:27:16,421 --> 00:27:18,087
and just dropped dead?

412
00:27:18,854 --> 00:27:20,354
Just live the way you always have.

413
00:27:20,554 --> 00:27:22,387
Don't make people worry for nothing.

414
00:27:23,621 --> 00:27:24,721
Gyu O.

415
00:27:30,454 --> 00:27:31,654
Would you...

416
00:27:33,754 --> 00:27:37,672
rather I lived the way I always have?

417
00:27:38,554 --> 00:27:39,887
What are you on about now?

418
00:27:44,421 --> 00:27:45,521
That's my boy.

419
00:27:46,254 --> 00:27:49,887
You really are the eldest son.

420
00:27:50,054 --> 00:27:51,578
Good lad.

421
00:27:53,621 --> 00:27:55,321
You've got some on you.

422
00:27:57,621 --> 00:27:58,954
My eldest.

423
00:27:59,654 --> 00:28:02,821
Gyu Yeong, the twins, everyone else...

424
00:28:03,287 --> 00:28:05,421
they say, "Dad, when will you grow up?"

425
00:28:05,421 --> 00:28:07,554
Telling me to get my act together
and live properly,

426
00:28:07,921 --> 00:28:10,187
always nagging and shouting,

427
00:28:10,187 --> 00:28:11,787
and getting on my case,

428
00:28:13,087 --> 00:28:14,654
But you're the only one...

429
00:28:15,141 --> 00:28:18,262
who understands and accepts me, right?

430
00:28:20,054 --> 00:28:21,587
Thank you, Gyu O.

431
00:28:21,932 --> 00:28:26,887
You've been special to me
since the day you were born.

432
00:28:29,187 --> 00:28:30,954
You're all I have.

433
00:28:32,914 --> 00:28:35,391
- Hold still.
- Let go. Just tell me. I understand.

434
00:28:35,754 --> 00:28:37,021
Let me hold you.

435
00:28:59,221 --> 00:29:00,254
You know me, right?

436
00:29:01,054 --> 00:29:02,487
No, I don't.

437
00:29:02,654 --> 00:29:03,787
You really don't?

438
00:29:04,187 --> 00:29:06,853
I said I don't. Who are you?

439
00:29:18,121 --> 00:29:19,187
Welcome...

440
00:29:20,187 --> 00:29:21,787
What is it this time?

441
00:29:21,787 --> 00:29:24,121
Did your sister leave
something else behind?

442
00:29:25,121 --> 00:29:26,454
It's nothing like that.

443
00:29:28,421 --> 00:29:30,487
There's something I wanted to ask you.

444
00:29:30,754 --> 00:29:32,554
Me? What is it?

445
00:29:35,987 --> 00:29:37,854
When I came to the shop last time,

446
00:29:37,854 --> 00:29:39,754
there was a young female customer.

447
00:29:40,320 --> 00:29:43,154
There are plenty of young women
who shop here.

448
00:29:43,821 --> 00:29:45,521
She seemed to know you well.

449
00:29:46,721 --> 00:29:48,954
I know plenty of people.

450
00:29:51,987 --> 00:29:53,754
She wore a sky-blue dress,

451
00:29:53,754 --> 00:29:56,154
with big eyes, and she was cute.

452
00:29:57,321 --> 00:29:59,821
She used to come by back when
you ran the food stall.

453
00:30:00,387 --> 00:30:01,854
Hui Na.

454
00:30:01,854 --> 00:30:04,629
- You must mean Hui Na.
- Yes, that's right.

455
00:30:04,654 --> 00:30:06,587
What about Hui Na?

456
00:30:09,987 --> 00:30:11,821
Could I get her contact details?

457
00:30:13,421 --> 00:30:15,754
She did leave her number,

458
00:30:16,554 --> 00:30:18,587
but I can't just hand it...

459
00:30:18,587 --> 00:30:20,421
to anyone who asks.

460
00:30:21,787 --> 00:30:25,221
Of course. You're not just anyone.

461
00:30:25,487 --> 00:30:28,021
I can confirm who you are.

462
00:30:29,421 --> 00:30:30,721
Even so...

463
00:30:30,721 --> 00:30:33,254
I won't do anything
to put you in a difficult spot.

464
00:30:33,254 --> 00:30:34,521
I only need to ask her one thing.

465
00:30:35,054 --> 00:30:36,287
What is it?

466
00:30:36,287 --> 00:30:38,021
What are you going to ask?

467
00:30:41,187 --> 00:30:43,021
Well? Out with it.

468
00:30:43,754 --> 00:30:46,054
I'm dying to know.

469
00:30:46,854 --> 00:30:47,854
Should I give it to you?

470
00:30:47,854 --> 00:30:49,921
All right, that's it for today.

471
00:30:50,021 --> 00:30:52,954
Wash your hands well and enjoy your meal.

472
00:30:52,954 --> 00:30:54,521
- Yes.
- Yes.

473
00:30:54,521 --> 00:30:57,629
Don't be picky.
Make sure you eat a balanced meal.

474
00:30:57,654 --> 00:30:59,921
- Yes.
- Yes.

475
00:31:09,887 --> 00:31:11,187
(Min Ju)

476
00:31:11,187 --> 00:31:12,454
In class?

477
00:31:12,454 --> 00:31:13,854
Big news.

478
00:31:13,854 --> 00:31:15,387
Call me as soon as you're done.

479
00:31:21,421 --> 00:31:22,554
What's the big news?

480
00:31:22,821 --> 00:31:23,954
Kwon Hui Na.

481
00:31:23,954 --> 00:31:25,921
That bird is finally out of the picture.

482
00:31:26,587 --> 00:31:28,221
- Really?
- Yes.

483
00:31:28,621 --> 00:31:31,421
The gigolo told my mom he was
breaking up and vanished.

484
00:31:31,987 --> 00:31:33,021
Incredible.

485
00:31:34,121 --> 00:31:35,854
Is your mother all right?

486
00:31:36,087 --> 00:31:37,654
Of course she isn't.

487
00:31:38,154 --> 00:31:40,621
She's been crying her eyes out
behind our backs.

488
00:31:40,887 --> 00:31:43,321
Anyway, it's a relief, isn't it?

489
00:31:43,821 --> 00:31:45,021
It is a relief.

490
00:31:45,387 --> 00:31:46,754
It's all thanks to you, Hui Na.

491
00:31:46,954 --> 00:31:49,754
I'll treat you to a proper meal
or drinks somewhere nice soon.

492
00:31:50,187 --> 00:31:51,854
Sure. Let's talk again.

493
00:32:02,721 --> 00:32:04,387
(That gigolo)

494
00:32:04,754 --> 00:32:06,587
He catches on quick,

495
00:32:06,587 --> 00:32:07,821
and he isn't stupid.

496
00:32:09,654 --> 00:32:12,321
Once you're off to Gangnam,
never come back, gigolo.

497
00:32:12,954 --> 00:32:15,021
You're permanently deleted.

498
00:32:15,021 --> 00:32:17,287
(That gigolo)

499
00:32:18,330 --> 00:32:20,487
What? Why is he calling me?

500
00:32:24,887 --> 00:32:26,187
What is this?

501
00:32:36,954 --> 00:32:39,421
(Kwon Hui Na)

502
00:32:44,454 --> 00:32:45,521
Kwon Hui Na.

503
00:32:45,854 --> 00:32:48,888
It's Han Gyu O. Do you really
not remember me?

504
00:32:49,321 --> 00:32:51,054
I recognized you at first sight.

505
00:33:14,221 --> 00:33:16,087
Why did this bird call me?

506
00:33:17,954 --> 00:33:20,654
To come after me for ruining his business?

507
00:33:22,221 --> 00:33:25,354
That's why I only used a payphone.

508
00:33:27,554 --> 00:33:28,754
Or could it be...

509
00:33:29,587 --> 00:33:30,954
Did he have my number?

510
00:33:32,721 --> 00:33:34,654
What do I do...

511
00:33:37,321 --> 00:33:38,554
We are sorry, Chef.

512
00:33:39,821 --> 00:33:41,954
We should have checked more carefully...

513
00:33:43,154 --> 00:33:45,721
We did notice it wasn't cooling
as well as usual...

514
00:33:45,987 --> 00:33:48,587
but the light was still on,
so we didn't think it was broken.

515
00:34:01,027 --> 00:34:02,227
This won't do.

516
00:34:03,754 --> 00:34:05,354
Tonight's service is the problem, right?

517
00:34:05,921 --> 00:34:06,921
Yes.

518
00:34:06,921 --> 00:34:09,321
What if we go without pickles today?

519
00:34:10,021 --> 00:34:11,054
What?

520
00:34:11,521 --> 00:34:12,554
That wouldn't work, would it?

521
00:34:20,254 --> 00:34:21,354
White kimchi.

522
00:34:24,054 --> 00:34:25,354
That place from earlier, Suragan?

523
00:34:25,554 --> 00:34:27,654
There's some white kimchi left
from what I tried earlier, right?

524
00:34:27,654 --> 00:34:29,521
- Yes, there is.
- Bring it here.

525
00:34:48,314 --> 00:34:49,381
Let's go with this.

526
00:34:50,954 --> 00:34:53,587
But the CEO said not to order
from Suragan...

527
00:34:55,046 --> 00:34:56,313
I own one percent more...

528
00:34:56,821 --> 00:34:58,721
of this restaurant than he does.

529
00:34:59,820 --> 00:35:02,637
- Where is this place?
- I'll find out right away.

530
00:35:05,158 --> 00:35:06,391
Welcome.

531
00:35:18,190 --> 00:35:20,424
So this is why Jeong Woo kept me away.

532
00:35:23,929 --> 00:35:25,288
What brings you here?

533
00:35:26,644 --> 00:35:27,864
I came to buy side dishes.

534
00:35:33,744 --> 00:35:36,580
Is this all the white kimchi
and radish water kimchi you have?

535
00:35:37,390 --> 00:35:40,297
There's more in the other fridge,
but it hasn't fermented enough yet.

536
00:35:46,878 --> 00:35:48,864
I'm a chef. I run the restaurant
just up the road.

537
00:35:49,388 --> 00:35:52,240
Our pickle fridge broke down suddenly,

538
00:35:52,265 --> 00:35:54,110
and the pickles we'd made
have all gone to waste.

539
00:35:55,861 --> 00:35:56,964
And?

540
00:36:00,271 --> 00:36:03,640
I'd like to serve your white kimchi
and radish water kimchi instead,

541
00:36:04,100 --> 00:36:06,536
so could I buy everything you have?

542
00:36:07,924 --> 00:36:09,631
I'm sorry, but no.

543
00:36:10,924 --> 00:36:11,944
Why not?

544
00:36:13,017 --> 00:36:15,337
Some of it is on order
for other customers,

545
00:36:15,444 --> 00:36:18,543
and the owner isn't here,
so it's not up to me.

546
00:36:19,791 --> 00:36:21,317
So you're not the owner.

547
00:36:22,158 --> 00:36:24,437
What's out front isn't on order, is it?

548
00:36:24,897 --> 00:36:26,278
Then sell me at least that much.

549
00:36:27,950 --> 00:36:29,695
Just buy it from another shop.

550
00:36:30,437 --> 00:36:31,619
Just sell it to me.

551
00:36:32,284 --> 00:36:34,037
I won't. Please leave.

552
00:36:34,084 --> 00:36:36,537
Why won't you? Isn't that
out there to be sold?

553
00:36:37,384 --> 00:36:38,850
I won't sell to you.

554
00:36:39,404 --> 00:36:41,871
- Please just go.
- Why won't you sell to me?

555
00:36:41,930 --> 00:36:43,257
I'm a paying customer too.

556
00:36:43,851 --> 00:36:45,908
A seller has the right to refuse service.

557
00:36:46,149 --> 00:36:47,397
Please leave.

558
00:36:47,422 --> 00:36:49,436
Why would you rather not sell to me?

559
00:36:49,636 --> 00:36:52,617
Do I have something on my face?

560
00:37:00,044 --> 00:37:02,364
Please go, before other customers arrive.

561
00:37:03,257 --> 00:37:06,264
I don't care if other customers come.

562
00:37:06,511 --> 00:37:09,510
Give me a reason I can accept.

563
00:37:09,557 --> 00:37:12,017
- Look here.
- Then you shouldn't make food...

564
00:37:14,131 --> 00:37:15,944
You shouldn't make it this good.

565
00:37:16,109 --> 00:37:19,212
You've ruined everyone else's taste buds.
Take responsibility.

566
00:37:28,323 --> 00:37:30,784
Who downs a glass of wine like that?

567
00:37:31,957 --> 00:37:34,223
I was so thirsty...

568
00:37:34,404 --> 00:37:35,975
Still, this isn't right.

569
00:37:35,977 --> 00:37:37,297
Our guest isn't even here yet.

570
00:37:38,210 --> 00:37:41,763
If my mom had seen that,
she'd have been appalled.

571
00:37:44,231 --> 00:37:48,033
A difficult patient
at the clinic really wore me out.

572
00:37:48,058 --> 00:37:49,688
And it upset me.

573
00:37:50,430 --> 00:37:52,716
So who is he, that you've arranged
a separate gathering like this?

574
00:37:53,011 --> 00:37:54,730
You two must be very close.

575
00:37:55,883 --> 00:37:58,976
We're not that close yet,

576
00:37:59,291 --> 00:38:01,093
but I hope we'll be close...

577
00:38:01,282 --> 00:38:03,297
for a long time.

578
00:38:03,784 --> 00:38:04,802
That much?

579
00:38:05,429 --> 00:38:09,144
If you say so, I'd better
make a good impression too.

580
00:38:09,251 --> 00:38:10,764
Yes, do.

581
00:38:10,789 --> 00:38:14,441
He's very particular about people,

582
00:38:14,442 --> 00:38:15,797
so don't get on his bad side.

583
00:38:17,677 --> 00:38:19,177
Just who is he?

584
00:38:19,643 --> 00:38:21,517
What makes him so special?

585
00:38:22,482 --> 00:38:24,004
You beat me here?

586
00:38:24,291 --> 00:38:25,737
I thought I'd come early.

587
00:38:25,762 --> 00:38:27,832
You're here? Captain.

588
00:38:29,590 --> 00:38:32,557
Getting married has you glowing.

589
00:38:33,750 --> 00:38:36,670
- I'm having a lot of work done lately.
- You look great.

590
00:38:37,877 --> 00:38:39,489
Is she the one you're marrying?

591
00:38:40,579 --> 00:38:42,184
Sweetheart, say hello.

592
00:38:42,531 --> 00:38:43,576
This is Heung Sik.

593
00:38:45,716 --> 00:38:46,876
Hello.

594
00:38:47,910 --> 00:38:48,933
Good evening.

595
00:38:49,201 --> 00:38:51,111
Seong Uk has told me so much about you.

596
00:38:55,217 --> 00:38:58,265
What are you doing, sweetheart?
Greet him properly.

597
00:38:59,236 --> 00:39:00,323
Yes?

598
00:39:00,710 --> 00:39:03,337
It's a pleasure. I'm Han Gyu Yeong.

599
00:39:05,196 --> 00:39:08,292
Why? Do you know each other?

600
00:39:10,437 --> 00:39:13,624
You look an awful lot like someone I know.

601
00:39:15,784 --> 00:39:17,172
It's a pleasure to meet you.

602
00:39:17,344 --> 00:39:19,151
I'm Cho Heung Sik.

603
00:39:21,346 --> 00:39:22,559
Wait, no.

604
00:39:22,917 --> 00:39:25,563
Looking closely, I do know you.

605
00:39:29,077 --> 00:39:32,155
But on second thought,
you're definitely someone else.

606
00:39:32,452 --> 00:39:33,848
- Let's sit down.
- Yes.

607
00:39:38,170 --> 00:39:39,357
A bottle of wine, please.

608
00:39:44,063 --> 00:39:45,753
Everyone, cheers.

609
00:39:58,529 --> 00:40:01,482
This wine is incredible. Truly good.

610
00:40:03,244 --> 00:40:04,338
By the way,

611
00:40:04,892 --> 00:40:07,250
you've hardly said a word.

612
00:40:07,697 --> 00:40:09,130
You're not unwell, are you?

613
00:40:10,337 --> 00:40:12,263
No, I'm fine.

614
00:40:12,418 --> 00:40:13,624
Exactly.

615
00:40:14,259 --> 00:40:15,903
You're strangely quiet today, sweetheart.

616
00:40:17,731 --> 00:40:19,428
I told her to make a good impression,

617
00:40:19,453 --> 00:40:21,498
so I think she's taken that
as her approach.

618
00:40:22,559 --> 00:40:24,930
It's all right, sweetheart. Say something.

619
00:40:29,017 --> 00:40:32,224
So how did the two of you meet?

620
00:40:32,644 --> 00:40:34,059
You two don't seem...

621
00:40:34,806 --> 00:40:36,320
to have anything in common.

622
00:40:37,166 --> 00:40:40,043
Let's see. When was it?

623
00:40:40,317 --> 00:40:42,804
Was it three years ago or four
when we first met?

624
00:40:44,543 --> 00:40:46,160
Four years ago.

625
00:40:46,443 --> 00:40:47,443
Four years.

626
00:40:49,046 --> 00:40:51,699
A younger guy I knew from the army
kept asking me to come,

627
00:40:51,724 --> 00:40:53,353
so I went to watch a yacht race,

628
00:40:54,094 --> 00:40:58,824
and there was Heung Sik,
winning the whole thing in style.

629
00:40:59,184 --> 00:41:02,733
I'd never had any interest
in yachts before that,

630
00:41:02,854 --> 00:41:05,390
but seeing him that day blew me away,

631
00:41:05,415 --> 00:41:08,110
I was so impressed
that I joined the club on the spot.

632
00:41:09,063 --> 00:41:11,990
Honestly, that day was pure luck.

633
00:41:12,893 --> 00:41:14,137
So...

634
00:41:14,883 --> 00:41:17,453
He entered a yacht race,

635
00:41:17,884 --> 00:41:18,917
and even won...

636
00:41:19,445 --> 00:41:20,445
Actually won?

637
00:41:20,911 --> 00:41:21,916
Really?

638
00:41:23,343 --> 00:41:24,343
Why?

639
00:41:25,784 --> 00:41:28,430
Do I not look like a man
who'd sail a yacht?

640
00:41:31,316 --> 00:41:32,770
Gyu Yeong, what's gotten into you?

641
00:41:35,591 --> 00:41:37,331
I just find it surprising.

642
00:41:38,377 --> 00:41:41,330
I look every bit like a freeloader,

643
00:41:41,416 --> 00:41:43,123
sailing yachts? It doesn't suit me.

644
00:41:44,158 --> 00:41:45,636
Very surprising, isn't it?

645
00:41:45,830 --> 00:41:47,456
No, that's not what I meant.

646
00:41:47,997 --> 00:41:49,584
Why are you joining in too?

647
00:41:49,911 --> 00:41:52,064
Where does a freeloader come into this?

648
00:41:53,744 --> 00:41:56,424
There's a girl I know,

649
00:41:57,884 --> 00:42:01,024
who calls me a freeloader
every time she sees me.

650
00:42:02,724 --> 00:42:04,184
Do I look that way to you as well?

651
00:42:04,831 --> 00:42:08,604
How could anyone say something
so rude to a fine man like you?

652
00:42:09,384 --> 00:42:10,418
Who is she?

653
00:42:11,086 --> 00:42:13,840
What sort of foul-mouthed girl
says a thing like that?

654
00:42:14,904 --> 00:42:19,337
Do I look like a freeloader to you too?

655
00:42:20,084 --> 00:42:21,235
No.

656
00:42:21,596 --> 00:42:24,299
- Something must be wrong with her eyes.
- Right?

657
00:42:24,447 --> 00:42:27,960
- She must have terrible eyesight. right?
- Exactly.

658
00:42:28,113 --> 00:42:32,444
And you just let her say that to you?

659
00:42:33,677 --> 00:42:35,144
What else was I supposed to do?

660
00:42:35,418 --> 00:42:38,210
Why? Do you want to call her
and give her a piece of your mind?

661
00:42:39,511 --> 00:42:41,510
Yes, let me do it.

662
00:42:41,697 --> 00:42:44,428
I'll call her and give her an earful,

663
00:42:44,724 --> 00:42:47,811
- so put her on.
- All right, hold on.

664
00:42:49,557 --> 00:42:50,997
Let's see, it starts with an "H."

665
00:42:51,110 --> 00:42:53,323
Her surname starts with an "H"...

666
00:42:54,147 --> 00:42:56,149
An "H"...

667
00:42:58,591 --> 00:42:59,597
Babe!

668
00:42:59,724 --> 00:43:03,357
Sweetheart, I'm so sorry.
Are you all right?

669
00:43:06,217 --> 00:43:09,891
I'm sorry. I'll just pop
to the restroom for a moment.

670
00:43:10,983 --> 00:43:12,317
Excuse me.

671
00:43:12,631 --> 00:43:14,150
Sweetheart, I'm sorry.

672
00:43:15,764 --> 00:43:16,764
Sweetheart.

673
00:43:18,751 --> 00:43:19,784
Have you lost your mind?

674
00:43:21,410 --> 00:43:23,076
You're the one who seems to have lost it.

675
00:43:23,964 --> 00:43:26,666
Seong Uk says the woman he's marrying...

676
00:43:26,721 --> 00:43:28,244
is the daughter of a businessman.

677
00:43:28,477 --> 00:43:29,710
How does that work?

678
00:43:30,350 --> 00:43:32,172
Don't meddle in other people's business.

679
00:43:32,211 --> 00:43:33,684
Did you lie, by any chance?

680
00:43:34,890 --> 00:43:36,564
What are you going to do?

681
00:43:36,770 --> 00:43:39,117
Don't you dare say anything
pointless to Seong Uk.

682
00:43:39,119 --> 00:43:41,310
Why would I say anything pointless?

683
00:43:42,690 --> 00:43:45,464
I could say something
that might actually help him.

684
00:43:45,489 --> 00:43:46,489
Heung Sik!

685
00:43:50,477 --> 00:43:52,964
I'm already about to lose my mind.

686
00:43:53,684 --> 00:43:55,370
Whatever you do,

687
00:43:55,651 --> 00:43:57,390
don't run your mouth
about my family or anything else.

688
00:43:57,470 --> 00:43:58,470
We'll see.

689
00:43:59,277 --> 00:44:02,304
When I say don't, you don't.
What do you mean, "we'll see?"

690
00:44:03,124 --> 00:44:06,636
What's the point of being so clever...

691
00:44:06,871 --> 00:44:09,490
if you can't read the room
or know your place?

692
00:44:10,877 --> 00:44:13,691
- What did you say?
- I hold all the cards.

693
00:44:14,150 --> 00:44:16,817
I'm the one calling the shots, not you.

694
00:44:18,329 --> 00:44:19,774
Depending on how you behave,

695
00:44:20,209 --> 00:44:22,938
I'll decide whether to grant
whatever this threat or plea is,

696
00:44:22,940 --> 00:44:25,244
or expose everything.

697
00:44:26,871 --> 00:44:28,710
so mind your manners from now on.

698
00:44:30,031 --> 00:44:31,031
Understood?

699
00:44:38,658 --> 00:44:39,664
Incredible.

700
00:44:43,243 --> 00:44:45,522
I heard Ung's grandmother
loves royal vegetable medley.

701
00:44:45,777 --> 00:44:48,417
I'll make some, so take it
with you tomorrow.

702
00:44:48,768 --> 00:44:52,169
Goodness, that's so much work
and trouble for you...

703
00:44:52,497 --> 00:44:54,955
Then let me pay for it in advance too.

704
00:44:55,182 --> 00:44:57,797
No. It's a birthday gift for her.

705
00:44:58,314 --> 00:44:59,701
Enjoy it.

706
00:45:00,931 --> 00:45:02,788
How can I thank you every time?

707
00:45:02,869 --> 00:45:03,970
Take care.

708
00:45:06,644 --> 00:45:09,118
- Good luck with sales.
- Yes, thank you.

709
00:45:09,120 --> 00:45:10,584
- I'll come tomorrow.
- Yes.

710
00:45:30,937 --> 00:45:33,390
Aren't you going? Don't you have
a business to run?

711
00:45:34,277 --> 00:45:35,377
I'll leave once you sell it to me.

712
00:45:35,551 --> 00:45:37,204
So I can get back to work.

713
00:45:37,504 --> 00:45:39,304
Why are you so stubborn?

714
00:45:42,391 --> 00:45:44,511
You're no pushover yourself.

715
00:45:45,871 --> 00:45:47,423
Fine, I'll sell to you.

716
00:45:47,591 --> 00:45:49,024
But just this once.

717
00:45:52,263 --> 00:45:53,844
That's not how it works.

718
00:45:53,846 --> 00:45:56,757
A customer decides what to buy.

719
00:45:57,837 --> 00:46:00,129
- What kind of nonsense is this?
- Nonsense?

720
00:46:00,870 --> 00:46:02,443
Why don't we go outside and ask people...

721
00:46:02,445 --> 00:46:04,470
who's being unreasonable?

722
00:46:11,743 --> 00:46:13,804
- What are you doing here?
- You're here?

723
00:46:14,397 --> 00:46:16,637
I'm having a dispute with the owner.

724
00:46:25,764 --> 00:46:27,530
She won't sell to me.

725
00:46:27,713 --> 00:46:29,150
Only to me.

726
00:46:29,323 --> 00:46:30,548
With no reason I can accept.

727
00:46:30,551 --> 00:46:32,368
She's incredibly kind to everyone else.

728
00:46:32,370 --> 00:46:33,629
She gives them extra side dishes,

729
00:46:33,654 --> 00:46:35,013
and even remembers their birthdays.

730
00:46:35,357 --> 00:46:37,891
- She's singling me out.
- You lunatic.

731
00:46:38,451 --> 00:46:41,851
If she won't sell, go to another shop
or just come back to the restaurant.

732
00:46:42,711 --> 00:46:45,036
What kind of scene is this
to cause in someone's shop?

733
00:46:46,137 --> 00:46:48,590
No. I'm not leaving until she sells.

734
00:46:48,617 --> 00:46:49,891
Why single me out?

735
00:46:49,892 --> 00:46:52,232
We need to hurry back and open.

736
00:46:52,537 --> 00:46:53,870
Are you really not getting up?

737
00:46:53,981 --> 00:46:56,084
Shall we tell the guests to eat air
instead of pickles?

738
00:46:56,086 --> 00:46:57,828
You can buy them from another shop.

739
00:46:57,831 --> 00:47:00,650
How can I go anywhere else
when nowhere else tastes this good?

740
00:47:04,094 --> 00:47:05,111
Here.

741
00:47:06,169 --> 00:47:08,937
I'll give it to you, so take it and go.

742
00:47:11,104 --> 00:47:12,477
When it runs out, I'll be back.

743
00:47:12,984 --> 00:47:15,364
You handle keeping him out.

744
00:47:17,597 --> 00:47:19,577
What am I, a ball he's supposed
to keep out?

745
00:47:19,578 --> 00:47:20,751
Keep what out?

746
00:47:21,911 --> 00:47:23,357
Keep your mouth shut, Kim Mu Jin.

747
00:47:25,117 --> 00:47:27,517
If you come again, I'll report you
to the police for obstruction.

748
00:47:28,110 --> 00:47:31,084
Go ahead. I'll report you
to consumer protection.

749
00:47:38,663 --> 00:47:40,117
Are you in elementary school?

750
00:47:41,026 --> 00:47:43,335
"I'll report you to consumer protection."

751
00:47:44,103 --> 00:47:46,558
- So childish.
- When did I?

752
00:47:47,019 --> 00:47:49,388
She's singling me out.
She won't sell to me alone.

753
00:47:49,413 --> 00:47:50,650
And you don't single people out?

754
00:47:50,817 --> 00:47:54,250
Our restaurant bans both dating
and married couples.

755
00:47:54,275 --> 00:47:56,975
That's one thing, and this is another.
They're not the same.

756
00:47:57,051 --> 00:47:59,304
So it's romance when you do it
and an affair when someone else does?

757
00:47:59,562 --> 00:48:02,884
Why are you slandering
the owner of that shop?

758
00:48:02,977 --> 00:48:06,539
She gives out freebies and extra food.

759
00:48:06,692 --> 00:48:07,927
Even things that aren't on the menu.

760
00:48:07,961 --> 00:48:10,670
Slander? Give out? Taking her side?

761
00:48:12,264 --> 00:48:13,737
Nothing like that.

762
00:48:16,190 --> 00:48:18,189
- You drive.
- You drive.

763
00:48:19,203 --> 00:48:21,097
Why did you buy a car
if this is how it goes?

764
00:48:39,084 --> 00:48:40,157
Mom.

765
00:48:41,364 --> 00:48:42,364
Gyeol.

766
00:48:42,991 --> 00:48:45,524
Are you all right?
I came because I was worried.

767
00:48:47,371 --> 00:48:48,404
Worried about me?

768
00:48:48,924 --> 00:48:51,844
In case you were still thinking
about what I said this morning.

769
00:48:52,104 --> 00:48:54,504
Honestly, I don't need a dad.

770
00:48:56,637 --> 00:48:58,481
- Really?
- Really.

771
00:48:59,377 --> 00:49:00,630
That sounds like a lie.

772
00:49:01,990 --> 00:49:02,990
Does it show?

773
00:49:08,564 --> 00:49:11,717
Give me some time to think
about the dad thing.

774
00:49:15,285 --> 00:49:19,044
There are plenty of good people
in the world besides Mu Jin.

775
00:49:19,337 --> 00:49:21,017
You don't like him?

776
00:49:23,031 --> 00:49:24,957
No, I don't.

777
00:49:26,016 --> 00:49:27,016
Mom.

778
00:49:27,931 --> 00:49:30,197
I'd rather we didn't talk
about Mu Jin anymore.

779
00:49:34,537 --> 00:49:35,944
Do you smell something burning?

780
00:49:37,004 --> 00:49:38,004
Why?

781
00:49:38,147 --> 00:49:41,059
Is my Gyeol's heart burning
with love for me?

782
00:49:45,224 --> 00:49:46,277
I left the seaweed soup on the stove.

783
00:49:54,650 --> 00:49:57,024
Mom, a wallet fell.

784
00:50:03,090 --> 00:50:04,531
What is wrong with me?

785
00:50:04,533 --> 00:50:06,811
If it weren't for you,
I'd have been in real trouble.

786
00:50:06,836 --> 00:50:09,609
Mom, did Mu Jin come to the shop?

787
00:50:09,744 --> 00:50:11,730
What? No.

788
00:50:11,937 --> 00:50:14,257
This looks like his.

789
00:50:17,877 --> 00:50:20,250
Yes, a little while ago, for side dishes.

790
00:50:22,192 --> 00:50:23,731
Give it to me.
I'll drop it in the postbox.

791
00:50:23,764 --> 00:50:26,917
I know where his restaurant is,
so I'll run it over quickly.

792
00:50:26,990 --> 00:50:30,483
Gyeol!

793
00:50:31,217 --> 00:50:33,772
- Is the army stew ready?
- Yes.

794
00:50:50,017 --> 00:50:52,265
I gave the white kimchi
and radish water kimchi to the kitchen.

795
00:50:54,039 --> 00:50:55,303
Aren't you going in?

796
00:50:57,569 --> 00:50:59,296
I don't think I can cook today.

797
00:51:07,976 --> 00:51:10,343
Let's raise the staff's pay.

798
00:51:10,591 --> 00:51:13,033
Do you know they've been doing
the work of a hundred lately,

799
00:51:13,100 --> 00:51:15,953
covering for you while you fall apart?

800
00:51:16,708 --> 00:51:17,777
I know.

801
00:51:19,784 --> 00:51:21,944
I was already planning to give them
all of my salary.

802
00:51:23,857 --> 00:51:26,303
Why do women like you?

803
00:51:26,328 --> 00:51:30,444
A man without a shred
of professionalism in him.

804
00:51:32,470 --> 00:51:33,632
Should I just emigrate?

805
00:51:33,846 --> 00:51:37,029
Did you plan this with Seo Hyeon?

806
00:51:38,818 --> 00:51:40,951
Seo Hyeon says she's emigrating too.

807
00:51:42,803 --> 00:51:44,228
Because of you.

808
00:51:44,349 --> 00:51:46,681
She says she can't watch
Kim Mu Jin lose his mind anymore,

809
00:51:46,706 --> 00:51:48,844
so she's going to the farthest
country from Korea.

810
00:51:51,004 --> 00:51:53,030
Tell Seo Hyeon to stay in Korea.

811
00:51:53,583 --> 00:51:55,649
Where would she go,
leaving her family behind?

812
00:51:58,031 --> 00:52:00,271
If anyone's emigrating, it should be me.

813
00:52:02,804 --> 00:52:05,846
Looking at your face, you mean it.

814
00:52:05,981 --> 00:52:07,351
Are you really leaving?

815
00:52:12,183 --> 00:52:14,016
I've thought about it hard,

816
00:52:16,776 --> 00:52:19,643
and I think the right thing
is to step aside and out of her life.

817
00:52:23,150 --> 00:52:26,241
What am I doing, throwing a tantrum
beside a woman who has a family?

818
00:52:27,836 --> 00:52:29,044
Aren't I out of my mind?

819
00:52:31,015 --> 00:52:33,728
I can't say that you aren't,

820
00:52:36,251 --> 00:52:38,926
but then that boy, Han Gyeol,

821
00:52:40,180 --> 00:52:41,863
is it over with him too?

822
00:52:45,917 --> 00:52:48,211
Yes, it's over.

823
00:52:49,767 --> 00:52:54,324
You'll never see him again?

824
00:52:57,256 --> 00:52:59,316
I won't.

825
00:53:00,230 --> 00:53:01,598
Mu Jin!

826
00:53:05,857 --> 00:53:06,863
Gyeol.

827
00:53:07,003 --> 00:53:10,392
I went to my mom's shop
and your wallet was on the ground.

828
00:53:10,980 --> 00:53:12,603
I came to bring it back.

829
00:53:14,463 --> 00:53:15,483
Thank you.

830
00:53:20,756 --> 00:53:22,750
How did you get all the way here?

831
00:53:22,910 --> 00:53:24,130
By bus.

832
00:53:24,937 --> 00:53:27,656
But why did you come to my mom's shop?

833
00:53:27,910 --> 00:53:28,950
To buy side dishes.

834
00:53:31,330 --> 00:53:36,004
Are you angry with me?

835
00:53:37,010 --> 00:53:38,017
No.

836
00:53:38,788 --> 00:53:42,497
Then why are you so cold?

837
00:53:42,677 --> 00:53:45,177
Me? I'm not.

838
00:53:45,370 --> 00:53:47,736
You're really strange today.

839
00:53:48,150 --> 00:53:49,971
Why aren't you smiling either?

840
00:53:54,170 --> 00:53:56,010
You're forcing it now?

841
00:54:03,431 --> 00:54:05,071
Just act the way you always do.

842
00:54:05,077 --> 00:54:07,531
You'll scare the boy into tears,
you lunatic.

843
00:54:16,227 --> 00:54:17,710
Have you had dinner, Gyeol?

844
00:54:18,869 --> 00:54:20,476
Shall we have dinner together?

845
00:54:21,671 --> 00:54:23,224
Now you're yourself again.

846
00:54:26,344 --> 00:54:27,517
You said you came by bus, right?

847
00:54:27,542 --> 00:54:28,714
I'll take you home.

848
00:54:28,904 --> 00:54:30,097
Thank you.

849
00:54:30,497 --> 00:54:31,516
I'll be back.

850
00:54:31,804 --> 00:54:33,901
- Goodbye.
- Take care.

851
00:54:36,057 --> 00:54:37,916
I found my wallet.

852
00:54:54,020 --> 00:54:56,930
Bye, Gyeol. Come again.

853
00:55:01,066 --> 00:55:02,736
Blood will out.

854
00:55:03,337 --> 00:55:04,910
Is it really blood, though?

855
00:55:09,409 --> 00:55:11,470
You startled me, Yun Jin.

856
00:55:11,711 --> 00:55:13,931
Who's that boy going with Mu Jin?

857
00:55:15,984 --> 00:55:18,457
Since when does he wear such a sweet look?

858
00:55:19,677 --> 00:55:21,230
Anyone who didn't know,

859
00:55:21,437 --> 00:55:23,103
would take them for father and son.

860
00:55:23,128 --> 00:55:24,136
Right?

861
00:55:24,937 --> 00:55:27,470
So you feel the blood tie too.

862
00:55:29,630 --> 00:55:31,096
What are you talking about?

863
00:55:31,799 --> 00:55:34,953
(Son)

864
00:55:42,583 --> 00:55:44,723
Why aren't you picking up, Han Gyeol?

865
00:55:46,450 --> 00:55:47,716
Hello?

866
00:55:49,530 --> 00:55:51,410
Dad, why are you answering Gyeol's phone?

867
00:55:51,831 --> 00:55:53,410
It was ringing, so I answered.

868
00:55:53,471 --> 00:55:55,663
He left his phone at home.

869
00:56:04,996 --> 00:56:06,883
Thank you for the ride.

870
00:56:06,971 --> 00:56:08,870
Sure. Get home safely.

871
00:56:09,777 --> 00:56:10,790
Han Gyeol.

872
00:56:10,815 --> 00:56:13,035
Gyu Seo. Gyu Min.

873
00:56:21,337 --> 00:56:23,221
Gyu Seo and Gyu Min?

874
00:56:24,209 --> 00:56:25,237
Yes.

875
00:56:25,563 --> 00:56:27,227
You're Mu Jin, aren't you?

876
00:56:28,189 --> 00:56:29,679
Yes, that's right.

877
00:56:30,739 --> 00:56:31,969
You must be Gyu Seo.

878
00:56:32,496 --> 00:56:34,482
- Have you been well?
- Yes.

879
00:56:35,417 --> 00:56:36,423
And Gyu Min?

880
00:56:37,737 --> 00:56:38,750
Yes.

881
00:56:40,716 --> 00:56:44,043
It's good to see you. It's been so long.

882
00:56:44,283 --> 00:56:47,278
I'd hardly have recognized you
on the street.

883
00:56:50,809 --> 00:56:53,623
- If you're not busy, can we talk?
- If you're not busy, can we talk?

884
00:56:57,430 --> 00:56:58,469
Me first.

885
00:56:58,817 --> 00:56:59,830
Me first.

886
00:56:59,977 --> 00:57:01,370
Just say it together.

887
00:57:13,270 --> 00:57:14,316
It's good.

888
00:57:15,097 --> 00:57:16,285
This is delicious.

889
00:57:17,260 --> 00:57:18,482
Have some.

890
00:57:20,292 --> 00:57:21,557
Thank you.

891
00:57:23,324 --> 00:57:24,355
All right.

892
00:57:25,149 --> 00:57:27,003
What is it? Go ahead.

893
00:57:30,051 --> 00:57:31,057
You go first.

894
00:57:31,517 --> 00:57:32,537
You go first.

895
00:57:34,651 --> 00:57:36,343
Then just say it together.

896
00:57:37,137 --> 00:57:38,510
No, it's not that.

897
00:57:39,187 --> 00:57:42,734
I heard you're still not married.

898
00:57:43,255 --> 00:57:44,257
No.

899
00:57:44,638 --> 00:57:45,910
Are you seeing anyone?

900
00:57:48,670 --> 00:57:49,676
No.

901
00:57:51,877 --> 00:57:54,223
You still haven't gotten over
Gyu Rim, have you?

902
00:57:55,144 --> 00:57:56,424
Han Gyu Seo.

903
00:57:59,275 --> 00:58:02,330
Gyu Rim has completely forgotten you.

904
00:58:02,903 --> 00:58:04,164
She hasn't.

905
00:58:04,353 --> 00:58:06,497
She still likes him a lot.
I know she does.

906
00:58:06,522 --> 00:58:07,830
What would you know?

907
00:58:07,844 --> 00:58:09,283
Gyeol told me.

908
00:58:09,308 --> 00:58:11,975
He said it seems like she still
likes Mu Jin a lot.

909
00:58:12,483 --> 00:58:14,285
It all ended eight years ago.

910
00:58:14,423 --> 00:58:17,109
You have no idea how hard
it was for her back then,

911
00:58:18,126 --> 00:58:19,476
how much she cried alone.

912
00:58:19,485 --> 00:58:21,577
Which means she liked him that much, so...

913
00:58:21,579 --> 00:58:23,045
I said it's all in the past.

914
00:58:23,703 --> 00:58:25,588
Her wound is finally healing,

915
00:58:25,638 --> 00:58:26,886
so why are you trying
to tear it open again?

916
00:58:26,911 --> 00:58:29,037
I don't want to see her hurting anymore.

917
00:58:30,157 --> 00:58:31,537
Stop fighting, you two.

918
00:58:32,530 --> 00:58:34,537
So what exactly is it you wanted to say?

919
00:58:37,324 --> 00:58:40,375
I'd like you to see Gyu Rim again.

920
00:58:41,177 --> 00:58:42,333
I wouldn't.

921
00:58:42,707 --> 00:58:45,856
I'd rather you didn't hang around her.

922
00:58:49,081 --> 00:58:53,137
All right. I understand you both.

923
00:58:53,983 --> 00:58:55,199
I understand,

924
00:58:56,814 --> 00:58:58,469
and I'll do as Gyu Min asks.

925
00:58:59,650 --> 00:59:00,905
After today,

926
00:59:00,960 --> 00:59:03,867
I'll never hang around your sister again.

927
00:59:03,892 --> 00:59:04,910
Mu Jin.

928
00:59:04,964 --> 00:59:06,084
Thank you.

929
00:59:06,931 --> 00:59:08,424
Find your courage again.

930
00:59:08,737 --> 00:59:12,029
Gyu Rim still hasn't gotten over you.

931
00:59:13,244 --> 00:59:15,319
I did lose my head for a moment,

932
00:59:15,780 --> 00:59:17,325
but I don't have affairs.

933
00:59:17,626 --> 00:59:18,661
An affair?

934
00:59:19,720 --> 00:59:20,722
What do you mean?

935
00:59:20,747 --> 00:59:23,275
- Your sister is married.
- She isn't.

936
00:59:23,664 --> 00:59:25,457
When did she ever get married?

937
00:59:26,431 --> 00:59:28,146
She never married.

938
00:59:28,148 --> 00:59:29,737
She's been raising Gyeol on her own.

939
00:59:33,510 --> 00:59:35,077
She isn't married?

940
00:59:36,797 --> 00:59:39,797
You lied about her being married,
to keep them apart, didn't you?

941
00:59:39,822 --> 00:59:41,682
To keep her and Mu Jin apart.

942
00:59:41,707 --> 00:59:44,753
I met him for the first time today.

943
01:00:17,075 --> 01:00:18,228
(Min Ja, my grandchild is my life now.)

944
01:00:18,361 --> 01:00:20,821
(My little angel is asleep. So adorable.)

945
01:00:35,164 --> 01:00:36,468
Chairwoman Kim,

946
01:00:39,214 --> 01:00:42,406
why do you keep sending me,

947
01:00:42,408 --> 01:00:45,310
pictures of your grandson playing, eating,
sleeping, and doing his business?

948
01:00:45,446 --> 01:00:49,058
How many of these are you sending
in a single day?

949
01:00:49,449 --> 01:00:51,156
This is violence.

950
01:00:53,757 --> 01:00:55,597
And honestly,

951
01:00:56,329 --> 01:00:59,640
Your grandson is only cute to you.

952
01:00:59,665 --> 01:01:01,764
He looks like a squashed bun...

953
01:01:02,890 --> 01:01:04,036
Never mind.

954
01:01:04,977 --> 01:01:07,163
Don't ever send me these again.

955
01:01:07,983 --> 01:01:10,575
Send one more and I'll block you for good.

956
01:01:11,881 --> 01:01:12,975
What?

957
01:01:13,000 --> 01:01:14,680
I'm mean-spirited?

958
01:01:15,677 --> 01:01:17,101
Envy means I've lost...

959
01:01:17,126 --> 01:01:18,141
You!

960
01:01:18,864 --> 01:01:21,497
Don't contact me for a while. Goodbye.

961
01:01:24,286 --> 01:01:25,924
That wretched woman.

962
01:01:26,183 --> 01:01:28,723
Her grandson is only pretty
in her own eyes.

963
01:01:28,943 --> 01:01:32,377
She's desperate to brag about him
to the whole neighborhood.

964
01:01:33,383 --> 01:01:35,950
As if she's the only one
with a grandchild.

965
01:01:36,450 --> 01:01:38,030
You don't have a grandchild, Mom.

966
01:01:39,297 --> 01:01:40,943
You're getting very cheeky lately.

967
01:01:41,644 --> 01:01:45,490
If you had one, you'd be far worse
than Min Ja is.

968
01:01:45,515 --> 01:01:47,555
Then go and have one.

969
01:01:47,710 --> 01:01:50,104
Have one and see how I'd be.

970
01:01:50,799 --> 01:01:51,817
No, thank you.

971
01:01:53,077 --> 01:01:55,183
Wouldn't it be possible with Mu Jin?

972
01:01:56,331 --> 01:01:58,784
I told you not to bring up his name.

973
01:02:02,469 --> 01:02:06,657
What would you do if Mu Jin
turned out to have a son?

974
01:02:06,682 --> 01:02:08,702
I said don't talk about him...

975
01:02:11,197 --> 01:02:12,617
What did you just say?

976
01:02:14,264 --> 01:02:16,437
Nothing is certain yet,

977
01:02:18,085 --> 01:02:23,030
but I think I saw Mu Jin's son today, Mom.

978
01:02:27,730 --> 01:02:28,736
What?

979
01:02:52,857 --> 01:02:54,071
Han Gyu Rim.

980
01:03:06,323 --> 01:03:08,036
I came because I have something to say.

981
01:03:17,611 --> 01:03:18,955
All this time,

982
01:03:21,536 --> 01:03:23,197
I've been truly sorry.

983
01:03:29,983 --> 01:03:32,153
I won't trouble you again.

984
01:03:39,197 --> 01:03:40,843
For as long as we live,

985
01:03:44,198 --> 01:03:46,517
let's never see each other again.

986
01:04:50,311 --> 01:04:53,098
(Love on the Menu)

987
01:04:53,177 --> 01:04:54,724
I heard you told him you were married.

988
01:04:54,750 --> 01:04:56,970
I corrected it and said you never married.

989
01:04:57,170 --> 01:04:59,756
So stop putting up walls
and stop running away.

990
01:04:59,884 --> 01:05:02,344
Just take the initiative
and do something about it.

991
01:05:02,623 --> 01:05:04,469
He got hurt because of me.

992
01:05:04,705 --> 01:05:05,729
Who did?

993
01:05:05,949 --> 01:05:07,604
I said I'll take responsibility for you.

994
01:05:07,650 --> 01:05:09,804
You shouldn't throw around
the word responsibility.

995
01:05:09,829 --> 01:05:11,529
I heard Gyeol's father is back. What now?

996
01:05:11,611 --> 01:05:14,764
What will you do if this boy
really is Mu Jin's son?

997
01:05:14,883 --> 01:05:16,996
We bring him home and raise him properly.

998
01:05:17,164 --> 01:05:18,170
You're not joking?

999
01:05:18,624 --> 01:05:20,437
- I'm not joking.
- What's going on with Cho Heung Sik?

1000
01:05:20,749 --> 01:05:22,004
Are you two dating?

1001
01:05:23,206 --> 01:05:25,106
Dramaday.me
